WEBVTT

00:15:25.954 --> 00:15:30.037
And, you know, I don't think that we have
to always operate like we're in a lab.

00:15:30.246 --> 00:15:32.204
Right, with a bunch of test tubes.

00:15:32.204 --> 00:15:36.121
But I do think that we should all be
running experiments in our lives.

00:15:36.579 --> 00:15:38.079
So during the pandemic, for example,

00:15:38.079 --> 00:15:41.162
I have instead of assuming there's a
routine that's going to work for me,

00:15:41.496 --> 00:15:43.287
I've run experiments to say, OK,

00:15:43.287 --> 00:15:46.537
what if I shift my creative brainstorming
from the morning to the night?

00:15:46.996 --> 00:15:48.329
What does that do, you know,

00:15:48.329 --> 00:15:50.912
to to the number of original
ideas that I generate?

00:15:51.704 --> 00:15:54.329
What if I turn my camera off
during a zoo meeting?

00:15:54.829 --> 00:15:58.287
Do I actually have, you know,
a more a more reflective,

00:15:58.287 --> 00:15:59.496
more thoughtful discussion?